# A write of a key that only a pattern constraint of the target matches. Only
# a field with a predictable name is declared (docs/translation.md, A4), so a
# lens writes such a key only with the struct that holds it, copied whole.
-- source.cue --
env: string
-- target.cue --
tags: [string]: string
-- lens.cue --
v0_0: _
v1_0: {tags: {env: v0_0.env}}
-- out --
not total
v1_0.tags.env is not declared by the target schema: only a pattern constraint matches it (rule target-undeclared) @ lens.cue:2:20
  help: a lens writes only fields declared by name: declare tags.env in the target schema to write it, or copy the struct that holds it whole
